1. GADS
-------

GADS (Globally Accessible Data Store)
https://github.com/ctrlo/GADS
Copyright (C) Ctrl O Ltd and the GADS contributors
Licence: GNU Affero General Public License version 3

The Go code is a port of GADS: its classes, routes, messages, SQL and
behaviour follow the Perl code, and doc comments name the Perl original.
Material taken or generated from GADS:

- upstream/GADS-dev and upstream/GADS: GADS itself, as git submodules
  (references to the GADS repository at fixed commits, not copies).
- gads-go/internal/db/sql_sqlite.sql and sql_postgres.sql: the GADS
  database schema, the tables that its DBIx::Class classes
  (lib/GADS/Schema) define, as SQL for each database.
- gads-go/internal/web/routes.go: the route table of lib/GADS.pm and
  lib/GADS/API.pm.
- gads-go/conformance/datasheet.go: a port of GADS's test library
  t/lib/Test/GADS/DataSheet.pm.
- conformance/results/perl*: output recorded from running GADS,
  including HTML rendered from its templates.
- The Docker image: the GADS views (views/) and public files (public/),
  copied unchanged from the GADS repository at build time. The public
  files include GADS's compiled JavaScript and CSS, which bundle
  third-party libraries under their own licences (see GADS's
  package.json), and fonts (Open Sans, Summernote's icons and GADS's
  linkspace-font) under their own licences.


